    amlo:productService amx:PS0129 ;
    amlo:technique amx:T0024 .

<https://example.org/amltrix/link/31b01287-5d43-4c74-86d3-59701e0e8ed6> a amlo:InstrumentLink ;
    dct:description """- Criminals deposit illicit funds in numerous small increments—each below local reporting thresholds—into multiple bank accounts. This prevents triggering automatic reporting mechanisms tied to larger deposits.
- They often coordinate multiple depositors, known as "smurfs," to spread these micro-deposits across different banks or branches, further reducing the likelihood of detection.
