    amlo:productService amx:PS0130 ;
    amlo:technique amx:T0098.001 .

<https://example.org/amltrix/link/5e8f277c-f8fc-4688-89ab-5b389725fe84> a amlo:DataSourceLink ;
    dct:description """Consolidated records of corporate registration, shareholder structures, and beneficial owners: 

- Reveals overlapping ownership or hidden ties across multiple entities involved in a single commodity transaction.
- Supports detection of shell companies and multi-layered intermediaries used to conceal ultimate beneficiaries."""@en ;
    amlo:dataSource amx:DS0049 ;
    amlo:technique amx:T0125 .

<https://example.org/amltrix/link/5e9905c5-6fed-4608-bb0d-0852db4b6fa8> a amlo:RiskLink ;
    dct:description "Criminals capitalize on the inconsistent or weak enforcement of sector-specific regulations across different jurisdictions. By forging specialized permits or licenses, they exploit these geographic blind spots or less rigorous checks, enabling them to bypass stricter oversight in one location and obscure the true nature of their illicit activities. This cross-border regulatory disparity is the primary vulnerability that underpins this technique."@en ;
    amlo:riskType amx:RS0004 ;
    amlo:technique amx:T0012.003 .

<https://example.org/amltrix/link/5e99a52d-a004-4528-988a-23412a942dfc> a amlo:ProductServiceLink ;
    dct:description """- Mules deposit or withdraw physical cash, enabling criminals to convert illicit digital proceeds into hard currency.  
