    amlo:productService amx:PS0130 ;
    amlo:technique amx:T0144.005 .

<https://example.org/amltrix/link/681401af-7b16-4415-a5d9-c85e2c0163a9> a amlo:ProductServiceLink ;
    dct:description """- Enable quick electronic payments to foreign chemical suppliers via digital channels, reducing transparency around fund flows.  
- Support layering by allowing multiple or frequent small transactions, making it more difficult for authorities to identify suspect payment patterns."""@en ;
    amlo:productService amx:PS0131 ;
    amlo:technique amx:T0142.001 .

<https://example.org/amltrix/link/681851ea-aa3a-447b-83b8-36fccd55ee32> a amlo:InstrumentLink ;
    dct:description """- Criminals establish or use offshore trusts in jurisdictions with lax oversight to handle illicit funds via trust accounts.
- By layering transfers through the trust structure, they obscure the identity of the true beneficiaries behind nominal trustees or shell entities.
- Rapid offshore transfers to and from trust arrangements further convolute the trail of ownership and purpose."""@en ;
    amlo:instrument amx:IN0030 ;
    amlo:technique amx:T0062.003 .

<https://example.org/amltrix/link/681ff9fd-599a-4fa9-910c-7b5089973a30> a amlo:RiskLink ;
    dct:description "After layering funds within casinos, criminals often leverage unregistered or lightly regulated remittance providers across different jurisdictions to move money internationally. They take advantage of jurisdictions with weaker AML oversight or looser reporting thresholds."@en ;
    amlo:riskType amx:RS0004 ;
    amlo:technique amx:T0011.003 .

<https://example.org/amltrix/link/6831b03e-0030-44f3-b4e0-7b11d8aff858> a amlo:TacticLink ;
    dct:description "By falsely labeling illicit proceeds as gifts, charitable donations, or other benign payments, criminals bypass standard due diligence and scrutiny. This misrepresentation allows them to open accounts, transfer funds, or conduct other banking activities without triggering red flags, effectively securing entry and continued access to financial systems."@en ;
    amlo:tactic amx:ML.TA0004 ;
    amlo:technique amx:T0040 .

<https://example.org/amltrix/link/68329ca0-9f05-4ef3-847c-3383efda8b15> a amlo:ProductServiceLink ;
    dct:description """- Criminals form shell companies and appoint nominee directors through these services to stage fictitious M&A transactions, obscuring the true ownership structure.  
