<https://example.org/amltrix/link/9cdecbfe-8838-46de-9d4e-ca52cc3c7503> a amlo:RiskLink ;
    dct:description "Ghost shipping exploits the inherent vulnerabilities of trade finance and related documentation-based products. Financial institutions often rely solely on bills of lading and invoices rather than physically verifying shipments. As a result, criminals can submit falsified records indicating cargo that never actually moves. This tactic enables the layering of illicit funds under the appearance of legitimate trade transactions, taking advantage of the product's document-centric processes."@en ;
