    amlo:technique amx:T0028 .

<https://example.org/amltrix/link/a2a07076-c3fc-41b4-822c-3d630f25292e> a amlo:InstrumentLink ;
    dct:description """- Documents such as documentary collections or bills of lading are leveraged to present a veneer of legitimacy, disguising repeated or circular imports and exports.
- These instruments help simulate authentic trade flows, enabling fraudsters to justify their VAT refund claims and obscure the repeated circulation of the same goods or services.
- By coordinating paperwork through multiple shell entities, criminals make it appear as if separate commercial operations are transacting internationally, when in reality, the underlying trades are largely fictitious."""@en ;
    amlo:instrument amx:IN0022 ;
    amlo:technique amx:T0144.007 .

<https://example.org/amltrix/link/a2b33ad2-3bce-4179-8c1c-df56ab7e391d> a amlo:InstrumentLink ;
    dct:description """- Criminals generate fictitious or inflated invoices (e.g., tuition fees, vendor services) to justify suspicious inbound payments.
