<https://example.org/amltrix/link/b9d4e9f3-740b-46f1-b263-b83e6227af76> a amlo:RiskLink ;
    dct:description "Commodity smuggling inherently leverages cross-border vulnerabilities, where inconsistent customs regulations, porous land borders, and uneven AML enforcement allow illicit goods to flow with minimal scrutiny. Criminals exploit these jurisdictional gaps to evade duties, obscure shipment origins, and layer proceeds internationally, making it exceedingly difficult for authorities to track illicit funds. This cross-border dimension is the central operational vulnerability exploited by this technique."@en ;
    amlo:riskType amx:RS0004 ;
    amlo:technique amx:T0048 .

<https://example.org/amltrix/link/b9eade7c-9b03-4022-9837-9e5ee1d2348c> a amlo:ProductServiceLink ;
