    skos:definition "An organization formed for philanthropic, social, charitable, religious, or humanitarian objectives, typically operating independently of government agencies. These entities often rely on donations, membership fees, or grants for funding and maintain financial relationships with financial institutions to manage their operational needs and disburse resources in pursuit of their mission."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://example.org/amltrix/scheme/amltrix-ml> ;
    skos:notation "AT0022" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Non-Profit Organization"@en ;
