        amx:T0090,
        amx:T0090.001,
        amx:T0090.002 ;
    amlo:shortDescription "Insurance policies, especially those with cash or surrender value, can serve as both legitimate stores of value and potential instruments for money laundering through their transferability and the ability to hide the origins of funds. Their recognized role in financial planning complicates detection, making enhanced due diligence and monitoring crucial for AML/CFT efforts."@en ;
