    skos:definition "Negotiable financial instruments encompassing both equity (e.g., company shares) and debt (e.g., bonds), representing claims on assets or earnings. Equity stakes may confer voting rights and dividends, while debt instruments earn interest. These instruments can be exchanged publicly on stock markets or transferred privately, and are widely used for investment, income generation, and capital preservation."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <https://example.org/amltrix/scheme/amltrix-ml> ;
    skos:notation "IN0019" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Securities"@en ;
    amlo:isUsedBy amx:T0011.001,
