    skos:definition "A financial service offered by banks and other financial institutions to electronically transfer funds between accounts, domestically or internationally. Typically facilitated through networks such as SWIFT, Fedwire, CHAPS, or SEPA, wire transfers are used for both personal and large-scale corporate payments."@en ;
