    skos:definition "Financial documents and agreements, such as letters of credit, bills of lading, and trade-related invoices, used to facilitate and secure international commerce. They often serve as guarantees of payment or evidence of ownership, thereby enabling orderly and secure cross-border transactions."@en ;
